Subject: No sprite-zero hit in the left eight pixels while sprites or background are masked there

AccuracyCoin's Sprite 0 Hit behavior, error codes 8 and 9; the test then stops at
code E, the hit's exact dot, which FCEUmm's line renderer does not time.
Checked with tools/accuracycoin.py --expect against the run before it, and
against the nes_bench checksums of Castlevania, Zelda and Chip 'n Dale.

License: GPL-2.0-or-later, as the FCEUmm code it changes (patches/fceumm/README.md).

---
diff --git a/src/ppu.c b/src/ppu.c
index 3cfba9a..f2c188e 100644
--- a/src/ppu.c
+++ b/src/ppu.c
@@ -476,6 +476,11 @@ static void CheckSpriteHit(int p) {
 	if (sphitx == 0x100) return;
 
 	for (x = sphitx; x < (sphitx + 8) && x < l; x++) {
+		/* No hit in the left eight pixels while either sprites or the
+		 * background are masked there (AccuracyCoin's Sprite 0 Hit
+		 * behavior, error codes 8 and 9). */
+		if (x < 8 && (PPU[1] & 6) != 6)
+			continue;
 		if ((sphitdata & (0x80 >> (x - sphitx))) && !(Plinef[x] & 64) && x < 255) {
 			PPU_status |= 0x40;
 			sphitx = 0x100;
